            <ArticleTitle>Giant coronary artery aneurysm formation following meningococcal septicaemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>300-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of coronary vasculitis with formation of giant coronary artery aneurysms in a child following meningococcal septicemia. We suggest that coronary vasculitis is a rare complication of meningococcal septicemia that should be included in the list of conditions known to elicit a Kawasaki-like inflammatory response.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
